    "text": "The WorldLines paper introduces memory-to-plan translation as a submodule within its architecture, not as a problem formulation for all embodied agents.",
    "topic": "Scope of memory-to-plan translation"
  },
  {
    "text": "The paper does not claim that memory-to-plan translation is a universal challenge; it is a specific mechanism to handle state reconstruction under partial observability.",
    "topic": "Universality claim"
  },
  {
    "text": "Memory-to-plan translation is explicitly a technique to reconstruct world states after memory overwrites, not a foundational problem statement.",
    "topic": "Nature as technique vs. problem"
  },
  {
    "text": "The paper's discussion of memory-to-plan translation is confined to its proposed system and is not extended as a general desideratum for all embodied agents.",
    "topic": "Generality of application"
  }
]
